data: {"sequence_number":537,"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_ce81c411-acfb-9dd9-909d-19af4eacb70d","output_index":8,"text":"**@nodejs profile:**  \nThe official X account for the Node.js JavaScript Runtime (@nodejs). Bio: “The Node.js JavaScript Runtime. 🐢🚀 Need help with Node.js? We've got a repo for that.” It has 919,243 followers and is Blue Verified.[[1]](https://x.com/nodejs)\n\n**3 most recent posts from @nodejs (as of Nov 9, 2026):**  \n- Nov 5, 2026: “Last week, the new Node.js 27 Alpha release upgrades V8 to version 15.6… New JS features and language changes, Performance improvements, Memory usage and GC changes, Diagnostic and tooling changes, Behavior differences… and more!” (https://x.com/nodejs/status/2118351099564335508)[[2]](https://x.com/nodejs/status/2118351099564335508)  \n- Nov 4, 2026: RT of @ljharb announcing nvm v0.41.0 with new `--only=alpha,lts,non-lts,iojs` flags (https://x.com/nodejs/status/2118096415100740088)[[3]](https://x.com/nodejs/status/2118096415100740088)  \n- Nov 4, 2026: “Yes we are!!” (reply in thread) (https://x.com/nodejs/status/2118039688158015748)[[4]](https://x.com/nodejs/status/2118039688158015748)\n\n**Summary of X reactions to the newest Node.js LTS release (v26, which went Active LTS on Oct 28, 2026):**  \n- Node 26 is now Active LTS (support until April 2029) and ships with the Temporal API enabled by default—no extra packages needed for modern date handling.[[5]](https://x.com/mo_claudius/status/2119495560080273737)  \n- Teams are being reminded to check their Node versions because Node 26 became LTS quietly, every future release will become LTS (no more odd/even rule), and Node 20 is already EOL.[[6]](https://x.com/thenamanraj/status/2119860069970141688)  \n- Some users report a gotcha: since Node 25, official Linux builds link against libatomic, which certain distros don’t ship, causing silent startup failures.[[7]](https://x.com/babak_builds/status/2117791187700748435)  \n- npm versions bundled with current LTS releases (npm 11.20 in 26, 10.9.9 in 22) still allow install scripts to run after a warning, unlike the stricter npm 12 behavior.[[8]](https://x.com/con_golias/status/2119031702546751675)  \n- Another security patch release landed for Node 22/24/26 on Nov 11, with limited details shared, prompting mixed reactions about maintenance overhead.[[9]](https://x.com/paraclyst/status/2118022255808557213)","logprobs":[]}

